# .trivyignore — accepted / triaged Trivy findings.
#
# Committed on purpose: this is config, not a report. It records HIGH/CRITICAL
# findings you've reviewed and accepted (e.g. no upstream fix yet, or not
# exploitable in our usage) so they stop being noise while staying auditable.
#
# One ID per line — CVE IDs (SCA) or Trivy check IDs (IaC/Dockerfile).
# Add a comment above each entry with WHY it's accepted and a review date.
#
# Example:
# # No upstream fix as of 2026-09; not reachable in our code path. Re-check monthly.
# CVE-2024-12345
